epo_name":"coollabsio/coolify","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:49:21Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"666ac84efbdd6468628465ecd0425d2f4c018c74","github_link":"https://github.com/coollabsio/coolify/commit/666ac84efbdd6468628465ecd0425d2f4c018c74","commit_subject":"fix(status): show running:starting while a health check is in its start period","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"vpnhood/VpnHood","commit_timestamp":"2026-11-03T19:49:01Z","branch":"develop","commit_sha":"0a5179e2c9929ec965871f3d3cfcab83ca2288e1","github_link":"https://github.com/vpnhood/VpnHood/commit/0a5179e2c9929ec965871f3d3cfcab83ca2288e1","commit_subject":"Apple TV: CLIENT's Apple TV app is Client.Ios.Apple's second target, no longer a head of its own. Client.Ios.Apple and Client.Ios.Extension target VhAppleTargetFrameworks - iOS, and tvOS in a build with -p:VhAppleTv=true, which needs the tvos workload, so every other build, CI's included, sees iOS alone - and Client.Tvos.Apple and Client.Tvos.Extension go. What the tvOS target takes apart: its own manifest, Info.tvOS.plist (AppBundleManifest), as a TV opens no file and no link; tvOS 17, the first with Network Extension; tvOS's own libsqlite3 for the split filters; and #if TVOS for the in-app review and the transport of an iPad app on a Mac. A tvOS build without the flag stops with the guard's message, now said before the package assets are read. A head with two targets has no platform in its outer evaluation, so Get-ProjectProperty takes a framework and Publish-IosApp.ps1 reads the bundle id with net11.0-ios: without it the id was empty and the publish would have stopped. Docs: the heads' READMEs (the Apple TV recipe now Client.Ios.Apple's), build-deploy-and-provisioning.md, the root props' comment. Checked on the Mac: the iOS target an iPhone and iPad app with an iOS extension, the tvOS one an Apple TV app with a tvOS extension, both started on a simulator, their API answering and their log without an error; CONNECT's iOS head builds as before.","